{"name":"Scuba","hex":"#6392b7","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"scuba","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An apparatus carried by a diver, which includes a tank holding compressed, filtered air and a regulator which delivers the air to the diver at ambient pressure which can be used underwater."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To perform scuba diving."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scuba"}],"entries":[{"title":"Scuba diving","blocks":[{"text":"Scuba diving is an underwater diving mode where divers use breathing equipment completely independent of a surface breathing gas supply, and therefore has a limited but variable endurance. The word scuba is an acronym for \"self-contained underwater breathing apparatus\" and was coined by Christian J. Lambertsen in a patent submitted in 1952. Scuba divers carry their source of breathing gas, affording them greater independence and movement than surface-supplied divers, and more time underwater than freedivers. Although compressed air is commonly used, other gas blends are also employed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Underwater_photograph_of_a_recreational_scuba_diver_in_Playa_del_Carmen_2006.jpg/330px-Underwater_photograph_of_a_recreational_scuba_diver_in_Playa_del_Carmen_2006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scuba_diving"},{"title":"List of in-memory databases","blocks":[{"text":"Notable in-memory database system software includes:"}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_in-memory_databases"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Underwater_photograph_of_a_recreational_scuba_diver_in_Playa_del_Carmen_2006.jpg/500px-Underwater_photograph_of_a_recreational_scuba_diver_in_Playa_del_Carmen_2006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipe